# file: internal/server/testdata/write_op_modes.golden
# version: 1.0.0
# guid: 656b77a9-3e50-456c-9945-dbbebbd7e041
# last-edited: 2026-09-25
#
# What `{}` does for every registered operation that can write (declares
# library.write, files.write or db.migrate, or declares no capabilities at all).
# Read by internal/server/write_op_modes_test.go
# (TestWriteOps_EveryWriteOpHasARecordedMode): every such op must have exactly
# one line here, and every line must name a registered op.
#
# Classes:
#   preview  omitted mode is a preview (owner rule 2026-09-25)
#   no-mode  the op has no preview mode at all; it always runs for real.
#            Known gap, docs/audits/2026-09-25-op-preview-default-inventory.md
#            section 5. Do NOT add a new op here to make the test pass: give it
#            a preview mode (opmode.ResolveDryRun) and list it as preview.
#
# There is no "live" class on purpose. A writing op whose omitted mode is live
# violates the owner rule; it gets a preview mode, not a ledger entry.
#
# Maintenance-job ops (maintenance.<job id> from internal/maintenance/jobs) are
# not listed: TestMaintenanceJobs_PreviewByDefault checks their advertised
# default against the job registry directly.
#
# Seeded 2026-09-25 from the inventory doc's sections 1-5.

